  "narrative": "All estimates and intervals are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive values support the registered claim and negative values oppose it. I did not reverse any signs. H66 is reassessed at its validation deadline. The discovery interval for PTEN loss among KEAP1-loss samples was 0.378 lower 0.193 upper 0.562, comfortably supporting the claimed stronger-dependency direction relative to the 0.15-unit threshold. Independent validation gave 0.409 lower 0.094 upper 0.724. That validation point remains above threshold and excludes zero, but its stringent lower bound is below the threshold, leaving some uncertainty about how large the subgroup effect is. I accept H66 as a supported within-dataset association with caution and close it rather than request further small-cell PTEN context tests. H78 is reassessed at its validation deadline. The discovery interval was 0.074 lower 0.010 upper 0.138, in the claimed male stronger-dependency direction but below the scientific threshold. Independent validation gave -0.013 lower -0.104 upper 0.077, opposite to the registered claim. I reject H78 as a scientifically meaningful sex association. H104 now has independent validation. Discovery gave 0.745 lower 0.666 upper 0.825 and validation gave 0.790 lower 0.683 upper 0.898, both far above threshold in the stronger-dependency direction for MSI-high among samples intact for TP53, SMARCA4, and KEAP1. This is decisive evidence that the MSI-high association is not simply a proxy for co-occurring TP53, SMARCA4, or KEAP1 loss within this dataset. I accept H104 and close it. H55 tests a positive Keap1-loss-by-TP53-loss interaction within adenocarcinoma. Discovery gave 0.274 lower 0.052 upper 0.496, but the lower bound was below the 0.15 threshold. Independent validation gave -0.134 lower -0.563 upper 0.294, opposite to the registered interaction direction and not supporting a meaningful effect modification. I reject H55 and close it. Final scientific report: the strongest supported within-dataset associations with dependency_composite are SMARCA4 loss with stronger composite dependency, MSI-high with stronger composite dependency, KEAP1 loss with weaker composite dependency, TP53 loss with weaker composite dependency, and PTEN loss with stronger composite dependency. The SMARCA4 association is very large and robust overall, in clean backgrounds, in adenocarcinoma, in adult samples, and within batch A; for example H4 is validated at 0.803 and H111 in a TP53- and KEAP1-intact background is 0.814 lower 0.768. The MSI-high association is also very large and now robust in the clean TP53/SMARCA4/KEAP1-intact context, with validated H104 at 0.790 lower 0.683; this strengthens the conclusion that MSI-high is not merely a proxy for the three strongest core predictors. KEAP1 loss is strongly associated with weaker dependency, validated at 0.795 in H13, and remains strong in clean backgrounds and batch A. TP53 loss is associated with weaker dependency, validated at 0.384 in H1 and confirmed at 0.402 in a SMARCA4- and KEAP1-intact background. PTEN loss is a smaller but still meaningful and independently validated overall association, H9 validated at 0.338 lower 0.198, and it is supported in clean triple-intact and KEAP1-loss backgrounds, though validation lower bounds in some subgroup tests are near the threshold. Negative or unsupported findings include the original weaker-dependency claims for KEAP1 H6 and PTEN H40, the MSI-high weaker-dependency claim H99, sex H78 after validation, and the adenocarcinoma Keap1-by-TP53 interaction H55. Many other single alteration, technical, media, library, batch, assay-availability, and constructed marker contrasts were rejected because they were below threshold or incompatible with the claimed direction. Remaining uncertainty is primarily biological mechanism, causal interpretation, external generalizability, and context modification. Some interactions and smaller PTEN contexts remain unresolved, and formal age, subtype, batch, library, or mutation-burden interactions were not all tested. These conclusions are associations among measured predictors in the supplied lung-lineage composite-dependency dataset, not causal knockout effects or claims of generalizability. The most informative next analysis is H118, MSI-high in the clean TP53/SMARCA4/KEAP1-intact background restricted to mutation_burden at least 5.0. H104 removes core-predictor composition as an explanation, but H108 used only a binary mutation-burden stratum rather than a combined context. H118 is the best registered test of whether MSI-high remains associated with stronger composite dependency after jointly restricting the strongest core predictors and a higher mutation-burden stratum. If H118 remains above threshold, the within-dataset MSI-high marker will be highly stable against major measured confounders. If it attenuates, MSI-high should be interpreted as biologically ambiguous and partly background-dependent. If it becomes available, validation should be reserved for H118 if it is accepted and near threshold, rather than repeated for already robust overall effects."
